  79:common/prog/ped_fw/stdcrc/StdCrc.h **** Crc16Result = CRC_Ccitt_Calc(8,Pointer);
  80:common/prog/ped_fw/stdcrc/StdCrc.h **** 
  81:common/prog/ped_fw/stdcrc/StdCrc.h **** For a big data areas is better to use partial calculation.
  82:common/prog/ped_fw/stdcrc/StdCrc.h **** 
  83:common/prog/ped_fw/stdcrc/StdCrc.h **** 2. CRC16 is possible to calculate over a specific data area partially by using function CRC_Ccitt_U
  84:common/prog/ped_fw/stdcrc/StdCrc.h **** it is possible to specify the length of data in bytes, which will be used to calculation.
  85:common/prog/ped_fw/stdcrc/StdCrc.h **** To use mentioned function, it is required to call CRC_Ccitt_Init() before the implementation and
  86:common/prog/ped_fw/stdcrc/StdCrc.h **** CRC_Ccitt_Finish() after the implementation to get successful result.
